\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces High-level three-zone architecture and end-to-end flow. Solid arrows are the forward path; the dashed arrow is the regeneration feedback loop.}}{5}{figure.2.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces Artifact lifecycle of a single request. The decision is computed on the synthesized template; a rejection feeds findings back into generation.}}{6}{figure.2.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.3}{\ignorespaces Hybrid deployment topology: AWS resources and on-premises nodes joined by an encrypted mesh, with on-premises nodes registered as SSM managed instances.}}{7}{figure.2.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.4}{\ignorespaces Regeneration loop as a flowchart. The loop exits on an accepting decision or when the attempt budget $N$ is exhausted.}}{12}{figure.2.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.5}{\ignorespaces Security-evaluation pipeline: parallel scanners, normalization to a common schema, cross-source deduplication, and aggregation by the risk-scoring engine.}}{13}{figure.2.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.6}{\ignorespaces The additive risk-scoring engine: four orthogonal sub-scores are summed and the total is compared against two fixed thresholds to yield the decision.}}{18}{figure.2.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.7}{\ignorespaces Runtime module dependencies. Entry points drive orchestration, which drives generation, evaluation, and monitoring; all external processes pass through the single execution helper.}}{22}{figure.2.7}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.8}{\ignorespaces Hybrid pipeline interaction sequence. The orchestrator gates both sides with the same engine, deploys each side only on an accepting decision, and emits telemetry.}}{25}{figure.2.8}%
